# Guide tile corner radius

Rounded content tiles (`.guide-tile`, `--guide-radius`) follow Apple Card’s `.tile` ladder — not a single fixed radius.

## Ladder (mobile-first)

| Viewport | `--guide-radius` |
|---|---|
| Default (phone) | `10px` |
| `min-width: 735px` | `30px` |
| `min-width: 1069px` | `40px` |

Source: apple.com/apple-card CSS — `.tile` uses `40px` desktop, `30px` ≤1068px, `10px` ≤734px.

## Always

1. Drive tile corners through `--guide-radius` (or the same numeric ladder).
2. Keep the three-step responsive radius when adding or cloning guide-style pages.
3. Use normal CSS `border-radius` — do **not** invent squircle / continuous-curvature shapes for web tiles (Apple’s site does not).

## Never

- Do not hardcode a single tile radius (e.g. only `28px`) on guide tiles.
- Do not use pill radius (`980px`) for tile/card containers — pills are for buttons only.
- Do not change this ladder casually to “look rounder”; match the table above unless the user asks otherwise.
